  "id": "need-for-achievement",
  "term": "need for achievement",
  "definition": "Need for achievement is an implicit motivational tendency to strive for excellence, seek distinctive accomplishments, and avoid routine. In this source, it is treated as one of the major motives that can shape behavior and, together with other motives, influence leadership effectiveness.",
